# README

## Project Compilation and Execution

This project uses a `Makefile` to handle the compilation and management of the build process. The following instructions will guide you through compiling, cleaning, and running the program.

### Prerequisites
Ensure that you have the following installed on your system:
- `make` (to use the Makefile)
- `g++` (or another compatible C++ compiler supporting C++17)

### Compilation
To compile the project, simply run the following command in the terminal:
```bash
make
```
This will create the necessary directories (if they don’t already exist), compile all source files in the `src` directory, and generate the executable file at `./bin/program`.

### Cleaning the Build
Before recompiling the project, it is recommended to clean up any previous build artifacts. This ensures that there are no leftover or outdated files that might interfere with the build process. To clean the build, run:
```bash
make clean
```
This will remove all compiled object files and the `bin` and `obj` directories.

### Running the Program
Once the project is successfully compiled, you can execute the program using the following command:
```bash
./bin/program
```
Ensure you are in the root directory of the project when running this command.

### Additional Makefile Targets
- `make clean`: Removes compiled object files and build directories.
- `make distclean`: Performs a more thorough cleanup, including removing the final executable.

### Notes
- If you encounter any issues during compilation or execution, verify that the required directories (`src`, `headers`) and files are present and that your compiler is correctly installed.

